AB  - Examined the therapeutic effects of a combined psychoeducational–psychotherapeutic group intervention in a pilot study specifically designed for schizophrenic inpatients. 121 Ss aged 16–47 yrs in Germany participated in a pilot study of inpatient group therapy comprising 12 sessions of psychoeducational training, 6 sessions of social skills training, cognitive training and various other group interventions and then rated Ss outcome by the Scale for the Assessment of Negative Symptoms scale (SANS, N. Andereasen, 1989) and the "Krankheitskonzeptskala" for schizophrenic patients (KK–Skala; Illness Concept Scale; N. Linden, et al, 1988). The results show a significant reduction of psychopathological symptoms, an improvement of treatment-related convictions and a reduction of subjectively perceived problems of all 121 Ss after the end of treatment. Ss with relatively more psychopathological symptoms and subjectively perceived problems showed the most impressive improvements after treatment. (PsycINFO Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)
