DO  - 10.1027/1618-3169/a000370
AB  - In a randomized controlled trial, we investigated the pattern of near    transfer effects of working memory (WM) training with an adaptive    auditory-visuospatial dual n-back training task in healthy young adults.    The results revealed significant task-specific transfer to an untrained    single n-back task, and more general near transfer to a WM updating    composite score plus a nearly significant effect on a composite score    measuring interference control in WM. No transfer effects were seen on    Active or Passive WM composites. The results are discussed in the light    of cognitive versus strategy-related overlap between training and    transfer tasks.
KW  - n-back task; cognitive training; working memory; near transfer
